proton-autogen (2.6.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New
    - New UX : proton-autogen --ux
    - UI/UX cleanup and improved GTK4 layout stability
    - Better separation between backend, UX, and config layers
    - Improved performance on game list rendering

  * Improve game scanning system (major UX improvement)
    - Limited scan scope to user directories only:
      ~/Bureau, ~/Downloads, ~/Jeux
    - Added excluded directories filtering (Backup, Windows dumps, drivers, etc.)
    - Added depth limitation to avoid deep legacy directories
    - Reduced scan noise from old archives and installer collections
    - Significant performance improvement on large home directories


  * Add Verbose option
    - proton-autogen app.exe --verbose
      Verbose output for debugging and diagnostics


  * Add game support:
    - Improved compatibility for legacy Windows games (Need for Speed series, RPG titles, etc.)

  * New utilities:
    - proton-autogen --help-env (new in v2.5.3)
      Environment variable reference (EN/FR support)

  * Patch:
    - proton-autogen --json-profile:
      export all profile environment variables in JSON format
    - proton-autogen --profile dx11:
      apply the selected profile type

  * User profile system (Pro mode):
    - JSON profiles stored in ~/.config/proton-autogen/profiles/
    - Allows per-game environment customization

  * --profile <name> option:
    - Loads and applies a user-defined profile at runtime
    - Safely overrides environment variables

 -- N3oray <n3oray77@gmail.com>  Thu, 27 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200
